  "type": "multiple-choice",
  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you have been tasked with configuring a session pooler service to optimize database performance for a high-traffic application that relies on Cloud SQL. Which of the following approaches to managing database connections will best ensure optimal performance and efficient resource usage with the session pooler service?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Configure the pooler with a fixed pool size equal to the maximum number of expected concurrent connections.<br/>B. Implement a pooler that disables connection multiplexing and maintains a fixed pool size.<br/>C. Utilize a pooler with an adaptive pool size based on the average number of concurrent connections.<br/>D. Configure the pooler to aggressively evict idle connections and set a high value for the connection health check frequency.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
